# Under the testing word WidenFlowNodes one result of a call or a read in four is given anything, as a larger program might give it. Under the checking word FlowMonotonicity Link runs on the program as it is as well,
# and the build stops by name (FlowNotMonotonic) where the tables from more say more than those: a rule that took something back when more arrived.
# function size(text) { return text.length; }  function note(value) { return typeof value === "string" ? size(value) : -1; }  function compute(n: number) { return n + 1; }  note(compute(1));  // forty times
# A TEST THAT CUTS EVERY ARRIVAL. As it is a number comes to note(), nothing passes the test, and NOTHING arrives at size(): its tables write no type, as they do where anything arrives. Given more, a text arrives there and is proven.
# That is no answer taken back: nothing lies within every type. The check asks the flow of the program as it is which of the two it was (ProgramAsItIsInLink) and asks nothing of a place that nothing arrives at.
# It stopped here with "f1: a parameter" until it did. The line `proven=string` holds only if one of the forty results of compute() was drawn, so the run is never the comparison of Link with itself.
# OPTIONS: testing=WidenFlowNodes:16 check=FlowMonotonicity
# STATISTIC: FactNodesWidened >= 1
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK: function f1 callers-known one-callee
# CHECK-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=string

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Integer integer=1
    v1 = NewClosure function=f3
    v2 = NewClosure function=f2
# REPEAT: i = 0..39
    v%(i*2+3) = Call v1, -, v0 calleeName="compute"
    v%(i*2+4) = Call v2, -, v%(i*2+3) calleeName="note"
# END REPEAT
    v83 = Undefined
    Return v83
}
function f1 name="size" module=m0 length=1 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="length"
    Return v1
}
function f2 name="note" module=m0 length=1 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    v1 = TypeTest v0 testedType=string
    Branch v1 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b2()
  b1(v2):
    v3 = NewClosure function=f1
    v4 = Call v3, -, v2 calleeName="size"
    Return v4
  b2():
    v5 = Integer integer=-1
    Return v5
}
function f3 name="compute" module=m0 length=1 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=number}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: number):
    v1 = Integer integer=1
    v2 = Add v0, v1
    Return v2
}
